Z||000000||LEE498||05-07-99||12:16 PM||||<br>Has anyone put a flowmaster on there fiero?If yes where did you get it and for what what type car? They don't make them for a fiero.I could have sworn I heard a cavilerZ24 with one.Whatever it had it was deep and hollow and it sound<br>very good.  
Z||000001||Shaun41178||05-07-99||09:41 PM||||Lee:  You can get a Flowmaster muffler from Summit, Jeg's or any local speed shop.  You need to purchase the muffler for the 82-97 camaro/firebird.  The price from summit will be $72.50 and the inlets and outlets are 2.5 inches in diameter.  The part number is FLO-42583.  You can get a free catalog from Summit by calling 1-800-230-3030<p>I just purchased one but have yet to install it.  I found a deal on mine and got it for $50.  I plan on a custom mandrel bent 2.5 inch from the cat back with some Borla tips.  It should give around 5-10  more hp.  I plan on a high flow cat as well.<p>Some others that i have talked to said that the exhaust note is a tad bit louder but still has a good rumble to it.  Good luck
Z||000002||LEE498||05-07-99||09:54 PM||||Thanks shaun!
Z||000003||LEE498||05-07-99||09:56 PM||||Thanks Shaun! 
